### Discussed in https://github.com/webpack/webpack/discussions/17777

<div type='discussions-op-text'>

<sup>Originally posted by **Bonnie-dot** November  2, 2023</sup>
Before  I don't use `type:module`, it can generate `manifest.json` and work well. But now I define `type:module` in package.json, I cannot generate manifest.json.
This is my config below
``` js
export default {
    entry: {
        vendor: ['react', 'react-dom', 'react-router-dom'],
    },
    mode: 'production',
    output: {
        clean: true,
        filename: '[name].dll.[hash:6].js',
        path: path.resolve(__dirname, 'dist', 'dll'),
        library: '[name]_dll',
    },
    optimization: {
        minimize: true,
        minimizer: [new TerserPlugin()],
    },
    plugins: [
        new webpack.DllPlugin({
            name: '[name]_dll',
            path: path.resolve(__dirname, 'dist', 'dll', 'manifest.json'), //manifest.json的生成路径
        }),
    ],
}
```
If you want to see the detail config, you can access the [repo](https://github.com/Bonnie-dot/demo/blob/main/config/webpack.config.dll.js)
Thank you very much for helping.</div>
